  "description": "SUMDIR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C226 H334 Eu2 O42 Ti7,C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti4 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti6 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti7 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti5 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.127-3.899 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.68-147.63°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Ti7(μ3-O)6(L)14(EtO)8; HL = 3,5-di-tert-butylbenzoic acid; possible dichloromethane lattice solvate of unspecified stoichiometry. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
